[7/92] GPQA Diamond/Physics Find KE of product particles in, Pi(+) = mu(+) + nu here Pi(+)
We have the decay:
π⁺ → μ⁺ + ν_μ  
π⁺ at rest, so initial momentum = 0.

Given:
m_π = 139.6 MeV/c²  
m_μ = 105.7 MeV/c²  
m_ν ≈ 0

By conservation of energy:
E_π = m_π c² = E_μ + E_ν  
By conservation of momentum:
p_μ = p_ν (magnitude, opposite direction)

For the muon:  
E_μ² = (p c)² + (m_μ c²)²  
For neutrino: E_ν = p c (since massless)

Let p be magnitude of momentum (×c). Then:
E_μ = √(p² + m_μ²)  
E_ν = p

Energy conservation:
√(p² + m_μ²) + p = m_π

Solve for p:
√(p² + m_μ²) = m_π - p  
Square:
p² + m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π p + p²  
Cancel p²:
m_μ² = m_π² - 2 m_π p  
=> 2 m_π p = m_π² - m_μ²  
=> p = (m_π² - m_μ²) / (2 m_π)

Numerically:
m_π² = (139.6)² = 19488.16  
m_μ² = (105.7)² = 11172.49  
Difference = 19488.16 - 11172.49 = 8315.67  
Divide by 2 m_π = 279.2 → p = 8315.67 / 279.2 ≈ 29.78 MeV/c

Then:
KE_μ = E_μ - m_μ = √(p² + m_μ²) - m_μ  
p² = (29.78)² ≈ 886.8  
p² + m_μ² = 886.8 + 11172.49 = 12059.29  
√ ≈ 109.81 MeV  
KE_μ = 109.81 - 105.7 = 4.11 MeV

KE_ν = E_ν = p = 29.78 MeV ≈ 29.8 MeV

Thus: KE_μ ≈ 4.12 MeV, KE_ν ≈ 29.8 MeV → matches choice B.

