[56/92] SuperGPQA/Engineering The transfer function of the system is g(s)=(s^2+3s+2)
We have  
\[
g(s)=\frac{s^2+3s+2}{s(s^2+7s+12)}.
\]  
Factor denominator:  
\[
s(s^2+7s+12)=s(s+3)(s+4).
\]  
Partial fraction form:  
\[
\frac{s^2+3s+2}{s(s+3)(s+4)} = \frac{A}{s} + \frac{B}{s+3} + \frac{C}{s+4}.
\]  
Multiply through:  
\[
s^2+3s+2 = A(s+3)(s+4) + B s(s+4) + C s(s+3).
\]  
At \(s=0\):  
\(2 = A(3)(4) = 12A \Rightarrow A = 1/6\).  

At \(s=-3\):  
\(9 - 9 + 2 = 2 = B(-3)(1) = -3B \Rightarrow B = -2/3\).  

At \(s=-4\):  
\(16 -12 +2 = 6 = C(-4)(-1) = 4C \Rightarrow C = 3/2\).  

Thus:  
\[
\frac{1/6}{s} + \frac{-2/3}{s+3} + \frac{3/2}{s+4}.
\]  
That matches option J.

Answer: J
