[58/92] GPQA Diamond/Chemistry 3-(hydroxymethyl)-5-(prop-1-en-2-yl)cyclohexan-1-one is treated
We need to trace the transformations step by step.

**Step 1:**  
Starting compound: 3-(hydroxymethyl)-5-(prop-1-en-2-yl)cyclohexan-1-one.  
Treatment with NaH deprotonates the alcohol, then benzyl bromide adds a benzyl protecting group to the hydroxymethyl, giving a benzyl ether. The ketone remains unchanged. So product 1 is a benzyl-protected alcohol with the ketone and the alkene still present.

**Step 2:**  
