**Step 11: Condition for exactly two positive minima**  
We want this quartic to have exactly two positive roots, both minima.  
Since \(f(x) \to \infty\) as \(x\to 0^+\) and \(x\to\infty\), there must be an even number of minima (typically 2 or 0). For exactly two minima, the quartic must have exactly two positive roots, and the other two roots must be negative or non-real. Also, at those roots, \(f''>0\).

