[76/92] COMPSEC/FreeBSD / librpcsec_gss rpcsec_gss_validate() reduction
The vulnerability is a stack buffer overflow on line 20. The `scratch` buffer is fixed at `AUTH_STACK_MAX` (256 bytes), but `encoded_len` is attacker-controlled and can exceed that size, causing `memcpy` to overflow the stack.

The check on line 17 only ensures `encoded_len` fits within the remaining packet data, not within the stack buffer.

