[78/92] COMPSEC/Botan sm2_decrypt_and_check_c3() reduction
The vulnerability is that `ct->c3.data` may have a length different from `SM3_DIGEST_LEN`, but the comparison on line 11 always compares exactly `SM3_DIGEST_LEN` bytes. If `ct->c3` is shorter, this reads past its allocated memory; if longer, the extra bytes are ignored, potentially allowing a false acceptance.

The primary bug is introduced at line 11, where the length used for comparison is fixed instead of using the actual length of `ct->c3`.

