[82/92] COMPSEC/Firebird xdr_datum() reduction
The vulnerability is a buffer overflow on line 10. The function writes a null terminator at `dst[n]`, but `dst` points to a slice within `base` with a specific offset and size. The check on line 6 only ensures `n` does not exceed available bytes in the XDR stream, not that `dst` has enough space for `n + 1` bytes within its slice. This can overflow the destination buffer.

